1
00:00:01,131 --> 00:00:03,832
[SPEAKER_00]: There's loads of questions, anyway, that I'll start with.

2
00:00:08,013 --> 00:00:11,734
[SPEAKER_00]: This Anupana Sutta, 118.

3
00:00:11,774 --> 00:00:21,757
[SPEAKER_00]: It says, the fulfillment of the Four Foundations of Mindfulness.

4
00:00:21,957 --> 00:00:25,858
[SPEAKER_01]: When you do breathing, it says,

5
00:00:28,740 --> 00:00:46,310
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, the being who abides contemplating the body as a body, ardent, fully aware, mindful, having put away covetousness and grief for the world, I say that this is a certain body among the bodies, namely, inner, outer, breathing, in-breathing, out-breathing.

6
00:00:52,774 --> 00:00:55,615
[SPEAKER_00]: So I say that it is a certain body among the bodies.

7
00:00:56,276 --> 00:00:57,036
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, there's a...

8
00:01:00,609 --> 00:01:04,272
[SPEAKER_01]: Quite a bit of a debate over that translation.

9
00:01:04,292 --> 00:01:14,659
[SPEAKER_01]: I remember Bhikkhu Bodhi and then, I think, Jnana Malatya, he was referring to it as a body of in-and-out breath.

10
00:01:15,059 --> 00:01:17,181
[SPEAKER_01]: Then another said, well, no, it refers to the whole body.

11
00:01:17,201 --> 00:01:19,903
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I said, well, no, it refers to the whole body of breathing or this.

12
00:01:20,483 --> 00:01:21,524
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it was never clear.

13
00:01:24,034 --> 00:01:39,592
[SPEAKER_01]: But in terms of the practice of the mindfulness of breathing, I think, maybe, maybe I didn't, but I think I mentioned that in the note citation, maybe you don't get that, didn't have that part.

14
00:01:47,987 --> 00:01:55,729
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, the mindfulness, yeah, the mindfulness of the in-and-out breath, in-and-out breathing is inseparable from the body.

15
00:01:55,789 --> 00:01:56,470
[SPEAKER_01]: It is bodily.

16
00:01:56,910 --> 00:01:58,150
[SPEAKER_01]: It's bound with the body.

17
00:01:59,331 --> 00:02:01,171
[SPEAKER_01]: So, one doesn't occur with the other.

18
00:02:01,872 --> 00:02:08,174
[SPEAKER_01]: You cannot possibly conceive in-and-out breath of breathing without conceiving the body.

19
00:02:08,194 --> 00:02:10,595
[SPEAKER_01]: And same, body means breathing.

20
00:02:11,495 --> 00:02:15,817
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you're mindful of in-and-out breath, then

21
00:02:17,291 --> 00:02:23,275
[SPEAKER_01]: That which is the body there at that time, is one among the ways of experiencing the body.

22
00:02:24,175 --> 00:02:25,496
[SPEAKER_00]: Body among... Yeah.

23
00:02:25,516 --> 00:02:26,417
[SPEAKER_00]: ...possibilities.

24
00:02:26,517 --> 00:02:27,077
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

25
00:02:27,277 --> 00:02:29,799
[SPEAKER_01]: Among all the possibilities you can experience your body.

26
00:02:30,379 --> 00:02:35,503
[SPEAKER_01]: Familiar, unfamiliar, far, near, heavier, light, whatever.

27
00:02:36,323 --> 00:02:37,124
[SPEAKER_01]: This is one of them.

28
00:02:39,685 --> 00:02:40,085
[SPEAKER_00]: Agreeing.

29
00:02:41,086 --> 00:02:41,927
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, the body of

30
00:02:43,219 --> 00:02:48,043
[SPEAKER_01]: The way the body is experienced while breathing, while being mindful of breathing, not just left while breathing.

31
00:02:53,506 --> 00:02:59,030
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't have time to refine my vision of the body.

32
00:03:00,511 --> 00:03:05,475
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yeah, that's because you're expecting to find something hidden there.

33
00:03:06,155 --> 00:03:11,139
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you need to, like, sharpen your binoculars to really see the details.

34
00:03:12,278 --> 00:03:14,259
[SPEAKER_01]: That is true only to a certain extent.

35
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:15,540
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't really work like that.

36
00:03:18,302 --> 00:03:25,466
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, sharpening the image means, like, clearing the vision, as you say, it means just finding more details about it.

37
00:03:26,507 --> 00:03:34,992
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can find as many details as you like, if you have no sight of the nature of that thing, which is on a general level, no details will help you.

38
00:03:39,509 --> 00:03:41,890
[SPEAKER_01]: So, again, what do you expect?

39
00:03:41,990 --> 00:03:42,810
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you hope?

40
00:03:43,950 --> 00:03:49,872
[SPEAKER_01]: What are you crave for, to find, when you look at the body, when you want to look at it even closely?

41
00:03:49,892 --> 00:03:50,112
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

42
00:03:50,172 --> 00:03:50,252
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

43
00:03:50,272 --> 00:03:50,653
[SPEAKER_01]: What's there?

44
00:03:52,873 --> 00:03:55,894
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know what I expect, you know.

45
00:03:57,335 --> 00:04:01,196
[SPEAKER_00]: But if I say, yeah, I want, okay, I'm going to look, be mindful of the body, you know.

46
00:04:02,496 --> 00:04:02,756
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

47
00:04:05,197 --> 00:04:05,457
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

48
00:04:10,010 --> 00:04:13,092
[SPEAKER_00]: Just, just... well, to become dispassionate towards it.

49
00:04:13,672 --> 00:04:13,933
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

50
00:04:13,953 --> 00:04:18,315
[SPEAKER_00]: To be passionate towards it.

51
00:04:18,756 --> 00:04:19,236
[SPEAKER_00]: No, why?

52
00:04:19,316 --> 00:04:19,576
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

53
00:04:20,417 --> 00:04:21,137
[SPEAKER_00]: Why is that a goal?

54
00:04:27,241 --> 00:04:28,322
[SPEAKER_01]: Why is dispassion good?

55
00:04:36,742 --> 00:04:37,342
[SPEAKER_00]: No, say it.

56
00:04:37,402 --> 00:04:37,882
[SPEAKER_00]: It's obvious.

57
00:04:37,902 --> 00:04:38,142
[SPEAKER_00]: Say it.

58
00:04:38,402 --> 00:04:44,825
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, to be free from that passion or depression, covetousness and grief of the world.

59
00:04:45,225 --> 00:04:49,027
[SPEAKER_01]: So, what are those covetousness, grief in the world and everything have in common?

60
00:04:49,647 --> 00:04:50,187
[SPEAKER_01]: Suffering.

61
00:04:50,227 --> 00:04:50,807
[SPEAKER_01]: Suffering.

62
00:04:51,668 --> 00:04:54,509
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the whole point is to be free from suffering.

63
00:04:56,710 --> 00:05:02,972
[SPEAKER_01]: But if your attempts to look at the body closer and closer and closer are frustrating you and making you suffer,

64
00:05:05,667 --> 00:05:07,308
[SPEAKER_01]: Then you're contradicting the whole purpose.

65
00:05:08,389 --> 00:05:12,371
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, we agree, mindfulness of the body will bring freedom from suffering.

66
00:05:13,072 --> 00:05:14,293
[SPEAKER_01]: But you have to find out how.

67
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:18,455
[SPEAKER_01]: Not just do it blindly.

68
00:05:18,515 --> 00:05:24,119
[SPEAKER_01]: And, yes, we agree, not being mindful and not keeping the precepts will certainly result in pain and suffering.

69
00:05:24,799 --> 00:05:25,580
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just obvious.

70
00:05:27,661 --> 00:05:34,526
[SPEAKER_01]: But when it comes to... Because you are doing the suffering, the suffering is not hidden behind some

71
00:05:35,856 --> 00:05:43,660
[SPEAKER_01]: Some distant, I don't know, stones that you have to all turn up and look underneath and find what's there.

72
00:05:43,961 --> 00:05:44,741
[SPEAKER_01]: You're doing it.

73
00:05:45,181 --> 00:05:56,868
[SPEAKER_01]: So, once you place yourself in certain amount of containment through precincts and kind of, okay, I practice, I'm making the effort.

74
00:05:57,726 --> 00:06:04,569
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, now within that, you actually have to sometimes turn around and look at what you're doing within that.

75
00:06:05,170 --> 00:06:09,152
[SPEAKER_01]: Not just keep going and looking out to find the cause of the suffering.

76
00:06:11,773 --> 00:06:12,953
[SPEAKER_01]: Because craving is done.

77
00:06:14,154 --> 00:06:15,094
[SPEAKER_01]: You're responsible for it.

78
00:06:15,475 --> 00:06:20,477
[SPEAKER_01]: And craving is the absolutely only direct... well, it's the direct and absolutely only cause for dukkha.

79
00:06:21,498 --> 00:06:23,278
[SPEAKER_01]: Craving means presence of dukkha.

80
00:06:23,679 --> 00:06:25,479
[SPEAKER_01]: Absence of craving is absence of dukkha.

81
00:06:25,539 --> 00:06:26,400
[SPEAKER_01]: Simultaneously,

82
00:06:27,342 --> 00:06:29,384
[SPEAKER_01]: No, no, no, no time lapse in between.

83
00:06:29,404 --> 00:06:32,106
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a simultaneously arising, simultaneously ceasing.

84
00:06:33,007 --> 00:06:39,914
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whenever there is suffering in regard to absolutely anything, even if it's your meditation, means craving is there.

85
00:06:41,195 --> 00:06:44,878
[SPEAKER_01]: So, initially, certain amount of suffering is inevitable.

86
00:06:46,179 --> 00:06:49,763
[SPEAKER_01]: When you put that container, the craving is still there, so you will suffer.

87
00:06:50,623 --> 00:06:54,104
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you just keep taking that for granted, you'll never recognize the Four Noble Truths.

88
00:06:54,124 --> 00:06:58,745
[SPEAKER_01]: So, after a while, within that container, you have to start saying, okay, this is not me.

89
00:07:00,025 --> 00:07:01,305
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm not doing anything unwholesome.

90
00:07:02,065 --> 00:07:04,066
[SPEAKER_01]: So, why am I still suffering within that?

91
00:07:07,246 --> 00:07:13,547
[SPEAKER_01]: When you recognize that the claiming is that dārtha, that directly is generating suffering, you stop doing it.

92
00:07:15,348 --> 00:07:16,648
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you'll know how to meditate.

93
00:07:18,571 --> 00:07:19,231
[SPEAKER_01]: And everything else.

94
00:07:20,012 --> 00:07:25,155
[SPEAKER_01]: And, by the way, ānāpānasati is taught to these sort of ones.

95
00:07:26,136 --> 00:07:27,657
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it doesn't mean you shouldn't be trying it.

96
00:07:28,237 --> 00:07:33,841
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, like, through trying that, you can, you know, come to understand these things I'm talking about.

97
00:07:33,901 --> 00:07:35,962
[SPEAKER_01]: But, you have to know that

98
00:07:36,566 --> 00:07:54,463
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you have to keep a goal in mind, because it's so easy to become, when it comes to meditation and everything, and obviously, because all of the contemporary interpretations and techniques and stages and attainments or whatever else they talk about, you kind of are always led to expect something.

99
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,061
[SPEAKER_01]: When you go and sit, you expect something.

100
00:07:58,182 --> 00:07:59,763
[SPEAKER_01]: I expect peace from meditation.

101
00:07:59,783 --> 00:08:00,543
[SPEAKER_01]: I expect this.

102
00:08:00,643 --> 00:08:01,444
[SPEAKER_01]: I expect that.

103
00:08:02,244 --> 00:08:07,788
[SPEAKER_01]: And expecting something, it's like waiting for something, doing it in order for something to arise.

104
00:08:08,128 --> 00:08:11,170
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly the type of wrong meditation that the Buddha condemned.

105
00:08:11,851 --> 00:08:14,613
[SPEAKER_01]: In that sutra, when he said, you're like a...

106
00:08:15,570 --> 00:08:19,032
[SPEAKER_01]: A monk premeditates, overmeditates, undermeditates, mismeditates.

107
00:08:19,252 --> 00:08:38,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Just as a hyena, like, waiting in front of a rabbit hole, or as a stork, like, waiting for the fish, just waiting and waiting, like, focusing just on one point, looking for other animals of prey, in the same sense, the monk sits and, like, waiting for something to happen in his mind.

108
00:08:40,443 --> 00:08:42,724
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's basically meditation today.

109
00:08:42,904 --> 00:08:44,445
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where it's told as meditation.

110
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:56,193
[SPEAKER_01]: And even if it's not explicitly defined, you will inevitably imply that expectation.

111
00:08:56,233 --> 00:09:01,514
[SPEAKER_01]: That expectation will be implied in whatever meditation you do, whatever meditation technique, whatever.

112
00:09:02,454 --> 00:09:06,775
[SPEAKER_01]: One thing they all have in common is, none of them will teach you understanding, because there isn't any.

113
00:09:07,575 --> 00:09:11,296
[SPEAKER_01]: They'll teach you a technique, they'll teach you a type of praying upon something.

114
00:09:15,713 --> 00:09:16,853
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, okay.

115
00:09:16,893 --> 00:09:18,154
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you pray upon something.

116
00:09:19,854 --> 00:09:22,294
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's what it comes down to.

117
00:09:22,614 --> 00:09:27,675
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, whether it's this, vipassana, that, you're just praying upon something, then you have this overwhelming feelings or whatever.

118
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:29,836
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yeah, I got it in a rose or whatever.

119
00:09:29,856 --> 00:09:34,157
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's all just, you know, you tickle your foot, it will start to itch.

120
00:09:35,637 --> 00:09:37,397
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you do this, it will result in that.

121
00:09:37,457 --> 00:09:39,738
[SPEAKER_01]: It absolutely means nothing in terms of understanding.

122
00:09:39,758 --> 00:09:40,738
[SPEAKER_01]: It's irrelevant.

123
00:09:42,292 --> 00:09:45,574
[SPEAKER_01]: But once you have the understanding, even if you do meditation, you'll be doing it rightly.

124
00:09:45,914 --> 00:09:47,355
[SPEAKER_01]: Whichever meditation you do.

125
00:09:47,375 --> 00:09:50,137
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you'll be doing it through the right view.

126
00:09:51,998 --> 00:09:58,181
[SPEAKER_01]: I, from the perspective of craving, and not craving, and I'll generate more craving, and I'll be independent upon craving expectations.

127
00:09:59,322 --> 00:10:07,647
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, you'll be, like, standing yourself even further in the path of non-suffering that you already understood.

128
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:16,182
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you know that suffering is... Because you know how suffering rises, you know how suffering ceases, so whatever you do, you'll be doing it for the cessation of that suffering.

129
00:10:27,404 --> 00:10:38,947
[SPEAKER_00]: Because when I was... say, if I focus on that earth element, and seeing the earth element just... it's just the earth element,

130
00:10:45,415 --> 00:10:47,456
[SPEAKER_00]: There's nothing more that can be expected from it.

131
00:10:48,037 --> 00:10:53,401
[SPEAKER_00]: It's quite, you know, in my experience, like I say, I establish a mind in this.

132
00:10:53,821 --> 00:10:54,421
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no...

133
00:10:54,541 --> 00:10:58,744
[SPEAKER_00]: I feel like, oh, this is... it's just the earth that it moves.

134
00:11:00,365 --> 00:11:02,107
[SPEAKER_00]: And establish your mind in that place.

135
00:11:02,227 --> 00:11:04,068
[SPEAKER_00]: There's nothing more that I can expect.

136
00:11:06,490 --> 00:11:12,494
[SPEAKER_01]: One thing that you can develop then, but I think that does not... it's not... cannot be done through craving,

137
00:11:13,991 --> 00:11:19,854
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, there won't be any expectation, there won't be any craving when you establish your mind on Earth.

138
00:11:20,455 --> 00:11:31,941
[SPEAKER_01]: But what you can do then is keep developing, practicing mindfulness in regard to the established mind upon Earth.

139
00:11:33,262 --> 00:11:39,185
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, I mean, like, hold it in your mind for as long as you can, as they do in those vipassana centers or whatever else.

140
00:11:39,745 --> 00:11:42,547
[SPEAKER_01]: But be aware of its persisting while changing.

141
00:11:44,068 --> 00:11:46,689
[SPEAKER_01]: of the arising thing, which is establishment upon earth.

142
00:11:48,210 --> 00:11:49,750
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yeah, there's nothing to expect here.

143
00:11:50,451 --> 00:11:51,491
[SPEAKER_01]: The thing is still present.

144
00:11:52,952 --> 00:11:56,133
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's still present, and it's still present, and it's still present, and it's still present.

145
00:11:56,613 --> 00:11:57,594
[SPEAKER_01]: Not equally present.

146
00:11:57,754 --> 00:12:04,776
[SPEAKER_01]: Other things start arising, but don't lose the sight of that establishment, which starts to act as a reference point.

147
00:12:04,977 --> 00:12:07,037
[SPEAKER_01]: It's there, while other things are arising.

148
00:12:08,018 --> 00:12:11,139
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, you're really experiencing things through that foundation.

149
00:12:11,839 --> 00:12:13,000
[SPEAKER_01]: Foundation of mindfulness.

150
00:12:13,658 --> 00:12:18,279
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is why they call foundations or references or whatever else, you know, translated.

151
00:12:18,859 --> 00:12:23,481
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you will see that whatever, that thing upon which you're established, will eventually come to fade.

152
00:12:23,521 --> 00:12:29,142
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you're aware, you know, you see arising and ceasing.

153
00:12:29,282 --> 00:12:30,702
[SPEAKER_01]: It's arising and it's cessation.

154
00:12:31,203 --> 00:12:34,723
[SPEAKER_01]: As I said before, arising is like ascension.

155
00:12:35,064 --> 00:12:36,404
[SPEAKER_01]: Cessation is like descent.

156
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:40,425
[SPEAKER_01]: So it's through arising, persisting while changing is manifest.

157
00:12:41,147 --> 00:12:43,449
[SPEAKER_01]: Through ceasing, persisting, while changing, is manifesting.

158
00:12:43,509 --> 00:12:48,392
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why three characteristics, but they're not linear characteristics, as they are translated or usually written down.

159
00:12:49,473 --> 00:12:55,677
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's arising while persisting, while persisting and changing, and it's ceasing while persisting and changing.

160
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:58,939
[SPEAKER_01]: Fading in, fading out.

161
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:02,102
[SPEAKER_01]: The identity of the same thing remains.

162
00:13:04,703 --> 00:13:08,206
[SPEAKER_01]: But in a way, it's not the same thing, because its intensity varies, changes.

163
00:13:09,180 --> 00:13:10,821
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, another thing has arisen.

164
00:13:11,562 --> 00:13:26,551
[SPEAKER_01]: But the thing is, with the establishment upon such a general phenomenon, such as Earth, or any other casino, you can just maintain that mindfulness throughout, in regard to anything, because anything that arises on a particular level, has the element of Earth in it.

165
00:13:28,052 --> 00:13:31,473
[SPEAKER_01]: And the sublime, the most supreme of them all, casino of consciousness.

166
00:13:31,533 --> 00:13:32,053
[SPEAKER_01]: Imagine that.

167
00:13:32,693 --> 00:13:34,454
[SPEAKER_01]: Anything that arises implies presence.

168
00:13:34,894 --> 00:13:35,294
[SPEAKER_01]: Anything.

169
00:13:35,394 --> 00:13:37,554
[SPEAKER_01]: No matter how subtle, how quick, how slow.

170
00:13:38,335 --> 00:13:43,796
[SPEAKER_01]: You establish upon the phenomenon of presence of anything, your mindfulness cannot lapse.

171
00:13:44,896 --> 00:13:50,878
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's actually maintained through the particular arising of various irrelevant things.

172
00:13:52,883 --> 00:13:56,724
[SPEAKER_00]: But is that, sir, establishing your mind on infinite consciousness?

173
00:13:57,164 --> 00:13:58,144
[SPEAKER_00]: Would that be the same thing?

174
00:13:58,164 --> 00:14:01,465
[SPEAKER_00]: Because then it does seem a bit easy, easier, should I say.

175
00:14:02,245 --> 00:14:05,005
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, because if you establish your mind on presence... Oh, yeah.

176
00:14:05,306 --> 00:14:05,686
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yeah.

177
00:14:06,146 --> 00:14:09,806
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I don't mean presence in a tree-hugging, new-aging... Yeah, just a...

178
00:14:09,886 --> 00:14:11,687
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean presence, phenomenological presence.

179
00:14:12,227 --> 00:14:13,327
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a present of thing.

180
00:14:13,387 --> 00:14:16,548
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever it's in front of you, a thing that has a reason, it is present.

181
00:14:16,808 --> 00:14:17,148
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

182
00:14:17,228 --> 00:14:22,129
[SPEAKER_01]: So within that, it's in front of you, you can be even more mindful and more established upon something more general.

183
00:14:22,859 --> 00:14:24,399
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you can get a search upon the Earth.

184
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:26,520
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the element of Earth is present through other things.

185
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:28,701
[SPEAKER_01]: It's quite supreme in regard to everything.

186
00:14:29,241 --> 00:14:33,202
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, there is more supreme in regard to the element of Earth.

187
00:14:34,743 --> 00:14:37,063
[SPEAKER_01]: And ultimately, it's the Consciousness.

188
00:14:37,484 --> 00:14:39,524
[SPEAKER_01]: It's the most supreme, the most refined.

189
00:14:40,564 --> 00:14:45,626
[SPEAKER_01]: But you don't have to go that far, because it's that reference point that matters.

190
00:14:45,646 --> 00:14:47,727
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what gets to me more, as well.

191
00:14:47,787 --> 00:14:49,927
[SPEAKER_00]: I suppose, it's my craving, because I...

192
00:14:52,883 --> 00:14:55,064
[SPEAKER_00]: I try to establish my own earth, and then, what is there?

193
00:14:55,104 --> 00:14:57,705
[SPEAKER_00]: It's just lots of water, and there's lots of fire.

194
00:14:58,285 --> 00:14:59,045
[SPEAKER_00]: How about some air?

195
00:15:00,686 --> 00:15:02,287
[SPEAKER_01]: How about some diversity?

196
00:15:02,647 --> 00:15:04,167
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then I think, okay, well... Well, that's the thing.

197
00:15:04,227 --> 00:15:10,070
[SPEAKER_01]: When that starts happening, it means you are not really established upon the element of earth, because you lost it so quickly.

198
00:15:10,650 --> 00:15:18,433
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you were established, if your mindfulness was set in it, then when those other cravings start coming up, you see them through this reference point, which you won't lose.

199
00:15:20,093 --> 00:15:22,936
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, if you start feeling, oh, what if I start losing this reference point?

200
00:15:23,217 --> 00:15:27,141
[SPEAKER_01]: You see that through the reference point of Earth, because it is within there, already.

201
00:15:27,642 --> 00:15:29,023
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's how understanding comes.

202
00:15:30,004 --> 00:15:31,586
[SPEAKER_01]: Through practicing that, while...

203
00:15:32,267 --> 00:15:33,789
[SPEAKER_01]: Remember, I was emphasizing that before.

204
00:15:33,949 --> 00:15:35,311
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the practice of mindfulness.

205
00:15:35,871 --> 00:15:40,356
[SPEAKER_01]: While two things simultaneously present, you become aware of that principle.

206
00:15:41,250 --> 00:15:52,292
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you do that long enough, you realize that the understanding will come, even if you don't go around experiencing every individual thing that can arise while you're established upon the element of earth.

207
00:15:53,873 --> 00:16:05,815
[SPEAKER_01]: You do that to a certain extent, but after a while it becomes apparent, you understand, you see through it, and you realize that whatever has arisen, whatever will arise, whatever is arising now, will remain.

208
00:16:09,419 --> 00:16:21,081
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's how that understanding kind of compensates, deals with it, fills up whatever else experience you were lacking in terms of insight.

209
00:16:21,281 --> 00:16:28,222
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, sometimes you need to go through these motions more before the understanding occurs, but eventually it should occur.

210
00:16:28,502 --> 00:16:33,343
[SPEAKER_01]: And when it does, then you will stop chasing particular things and stop being concerned about them, because you understood

211
00:16:34,096 --> 00:16:36,597
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever comes in, whatever goes out, has to come through at this point.

212
00:16:38,659 --> 00:16:39,459
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what matters.

213
00:16:39,559 --> 00:16:41,460
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter if a particular thing never mattered.

214
00:16:43,341 --> 00:16:46,983
[SPEAKER_01]: It was that relationship that you were not aware of.

215
00:16:47,163 --> 00:16:53,427
[SPEAKER_01]: It hasn't been understood, which was inducing all sorts of emotions and cravings and feelings and confusions and five hindrances.

216
00:16:54,448 --> 00:16:59,170
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, I'll experience...

217
00:16:59,190 --> 00:17:00,491
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll be the experiencing rapture.

218
00:17:02,656 --> 00:17:12,825
[SPEAKER_00]: I say that this is a certain feeling among feelings, namely giving close attention to in-and-out breathing, a certain feeling amongst feelings.

219
00:17:13,946 --> 00:17:22,994
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, giving close attention, I don't know, like, we will have to really look into a file in there, see the translation, but anyway, I can still answer it.

220
00:17:25,238 --> 00:17:34,685
[SPEAKER_01]: The whole point, the whole point, say, say you understood the craving, you soon found all the truths, so you, you are at least a sotāpanna.

221
00:17:35,826 --> 00:17:38,228
[SPEAKER_01]: You practice mindfulness of breathing.

222
00:17:38,248 --> 00:17:40,730
[SPEAKER_01]: So, breathing is bodily.

223
00:17:44,272 --> 00:17:47,575
[SPEAKER_01]: It's an intentional act that belongs to the body.

224
00:17:50,437 --> 00:17:50,657
[SPEAKER_01]: So,

225
00:17:57,595 --> 00:18:15,708
[SPEAKER_01]: So, with the lack of mindfulness and with the lack of knowledge, that bodily act is appropriated either through I am reading forcefully or voluntarily,

226
00:18:16,937 --> 00:18:24,163
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, through complete ignorance of that breathing, whereby you think it's completely automatic, so you obscure the fact that it is intentional.

227
00:18:27,526 --> 00:18:38,556
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you don't do either, you can actually come to see that breathing is an intentional act being done right here, that doesn't belong to you.

228
00:18:42,427 --> 00:18:48,551
[SPEAKER_01]: And there isn't anything more you can ask for, in terms of... in terms of a meditation object, inverted commas.

229
00:18:49,452 --> 00:18:59,218
[SPEAKER_01]: You have an act being done right here, right now, intentional act, not involuntary, like a heartbeat or something like that.

230
00:18:59,338 --> 00:19:02,300
[SPEAKER_01]: Yet, it doesn't belong to you, it belongs to the body.

231
00:19:03,681 --> 00:19:05,402
[SPEAKER_01]: You become established in that, then

232
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:13,846
[SPEAKER_01]: That body there will be one among the bodies which you're experiencing, but it will be the body that matters, it will be the body that is not yours.

233
00:19:15,107 --> 00:19:29,459
[SPEAKER_01]: That feeling there, looking at that type of intentional breathing that doesn't belong to you, that feeling you have there at that time in regard to that, will be one among feelings that you can experience, but it will be the one that matters, because it will be a feeling that is not yours.

234
00:19:30,240 --> 00:19:33,863
[SPEAKER_01]: That intention there, and we're saying for all the aggregates,

235
00:19:35,499 --> 00:19:48,046
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's why it will have to, if done properly with the right view, it will have to culminate in the full development of the enlightenment factors, the four powers and then the enlightenment factors.

236
00:19:50,988 --> 00:19:53,229
[SPEAKER_01]: Because we just reveal the whole thing as it is.

237
00:19:56,272 --> 00:19:57,552
[SPEAKER_01]: But it has to come through that.

238
00:19:57,972 --> 00:20:01,753
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you say, I am breathing in, like, as if you're doing it.

239
00:20:02,193 --> 00:20:10,915
[SPEAKER_01]: You start doing it, just to become apparent that, yes, you are doing it, and that whole thing is not yours, it's bodily.

240
00:20:14,716 --> 00:20:17,417
[SPEAKER_01]: So, everything remains the same, so to speak.

241
00:20:17,477 --> 00:20:23,118
[SPEAKER_01]: Just the emphasis of, I am breathing, bodily intention shifts onto the body.

242
00:20:24,170 --> 00:20:29,756
[SPEAKER_01]: So, I am breathing bodily intention, but now it's resting on the body.

243
00:20:30,097 --> 00:20:34,982
[SPEAKER_01]: So, even that I am breathing ceases to be yours, ceases to be mine, ceases to be me.

244
00:20:36,884 --> 00:20:37,224
[SPEAKER_01]: And then...

245
00:20:38,305 --> 00:20:49,753
[SPEAKER_01]: You become really established, then you go, I'm breathing in like this, I'm breathing in like that, I'll be breathing in like this, I'll be breathing in like that, I'll be feeling this, I'll be feeling that, I'll be doing this, I'll be doing... You can do whatever you like, because none of it belongs to you.

246
00:20:50,254 --> 00:20:56,098
[SPEAKER_01]: And by practicing it like that, you're just kind of reinforcing that recognition, that it's not yours.

247
00:21:07,228 --> 00:21:13,110
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, yeah, it's just in... it's inferior to the whole body.

248
00:21:13,590 --> 00:21:16,431
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, yeah, none of it would be there if that body is not there.

249
00:21:17,111 --> 00:21:19,872
[SPEAKER_01]: If that body is not intentional to begin with.

250
00:21:21,852 --> 00:21:28,814
[SPEAKER_01]: If there is no intentionality belonging to the body, in regard to the body, none of this would be perceivable.

251
00:21:29,554 --> 00:21:31,375
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's just that you appropriate intentionality.

252
00:21:32,288 --> 00:21:34,568
[SPEAKER_01]: Because that's mental, belongs... pertains to the mind.

253
00:21:34,588 --> 00:21:43,790
[SPEAKER_01]: And the Buddha said it's much harder... Well, it's easier to see body as not yours and get... get dispassion in regards to it and so on... in regard to it.

254
00:21:44,570 --> 00:21:51,491
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's much harder to... to feel the same towards your mind, because it's subtler, faster, harder to recognize and so on.

255
00:21:53,252 --> 00:21:56,292
[SPEAKER_01]: But mind is inconceivable without the body.

256
00:21:56,312 --> 00:22:00,133
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no consciousness juxtaposed over the body.

257
00:22:00,173 --> 00:22:01,313
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's not paired with it,

258
00:22:03,220 --> 00:22:05,842
[SPEAKER_01]: There wouldn't be nāmarūpa, viññāṇa, nāmarūpa, just wouldn't exist.

259
00:22:09,125 --> 00:22:23,898
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why this whole... the elements and body contemplation, just to reveal the subordinate position of the greatest of your thoughts and mind and... Yeah, the mind comes first, in terms of determining things.

260
00:22:25,459 --> 00:22:29,683
[SPEAKER_01]: But the order of form being first, structurally, cannot ever change.

261
00:22:31,708 --> 00:22:44,183
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as an act, for an action, the mind determines it, but structurally speaking, it's all dependent upon this conscious body, like matter that is paired with consciousness out there.

262
00:22:49,189 --> 00:22:49,890
[SPEAKER_01]: Conscious matter.

263
00:22:54,437 --> 00:23:01,039
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, when you think consciousness, you kind of imply it's inside, on this end of the spectrum, and the matter is out there in the world.

264
00:23:01,199 --> 00:23:04,379
[SPEAKER_01]: Actually, both consciousness and the matter are out there in the world.

265
00:23:04,999 --> 00:23:06,680
[SPEAKER_01]: Your consciousness is there without thinking.

266
00:23:06,740 --> 00:23:19,603
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you can even... Well, that's why you can perceive distances and space, but above all, that's why you can think in terms of space and in terms of distances, because consciousness is already there.

267
00:23:20,672 --> 00:23:21,772
[SPEAKER_01]: And it goes into infinity.

268
00:23:21,792 --> 00:23:26,614
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where you can perceive into infinity, if you're able to reach it.

269
00:23:29,935 --> 00:23:39,557
[SPEAKER_01]: The idea, just the thought of space, will be inconceivable if consciousness is generally inside of you, or in your head, as opposed to the matter out there.

270
00:23:39,577 --> 00:23:41,018
[SPEAKER_01]: It will be just a perfect linear

271
00:23:42,842 --> 00:23:43,363
[SPEAKER_00]: Flat.

272
00:23:43,983 --> 00:23:48,567
[SPEAKER_00]: But it's not... Is it one... would you say that it's one presence?

273
00:23:48,767 --> 00:23:49,087
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

274
00:23:49,888 --> 00:23:52,310
[SPEAKER_01]: As many forms as many consciousness.

275
00:23:52,450 --> 00:23:52,951
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the thing.

276
00:23:53,491 --> 00:23:53,811
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean...

277
00:23:53,871 --> 00:23:55,172
[SPEAKER_01]: If it's one, then it's mine.

278
00:23:55,913 --> 00:23:58,115
[SPEAKER_01]: If there are six, which one is yours then?

279
00:23:59,416 --> 00:24:00,136
[SPEAKER_01]: And there are six.

280
00:24:00,417 --> 00:24:03,319
[SPEAKER_01]: Each domain of the senses has its own consciousness.

281
00:24:04,280 --> 00:24:06,521
[SPEAKER_01]: Thus, each particular...

282
00:24:06,621 --> 00:24:10,565
[SPEAKER_01]: Within that, you have each particular consciousness within the same nature of consciousness.

283
00:24:11,422 --> 00:24:16,387
[SPEAKER_01]: That's all those divisions, like 6, 18, 108, or feelings, or this, or this.

284
00:24:16,987 --> 00:24:17,468
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how it goes.

285
00:24:17,488 --> 00:24:18,169
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not linear.

286
00:24:18,229 --> 00:24:20,311
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not like commentators try to list them all up.

287
00:24:20,491 --> 00:24:20,731
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

288
00:24:22,913 --> 00:24:27,157
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, there is, as an aggregate, as a nature of consciousness, there is consciousness.

289
00:24:28,298 --> 00:24:31,582
[SPEAKER_01]: But in terms of experience, there's six domains of your senses.

290
00:24:32,342 --> 00:24:34,785
[SPEAKER_01]: That's six consciousness, six different consciousness.

291
00:24:35,998 --> 00:24:49,002
[SPEAKER_01]: Just recognizing that can be enough for dispassion and abandoning the right view, because if there are six simultaneously present conscious domains, well, none of them, well, certainly not all of them, can be mine.

292
00:24:49,843 --> 00:24:55,745
[SPEAKER_01]: And if there is no feeling of singularity, like one, me, there is no feeling of self and mastery.

293
00:24:57,105 --> 00:24:58,526
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if there are six, well...

294
00:25:00,386 --> 00:25:01,127
[SPEAKER_01]: Which one is it then?

295
00:25:02,047 --> 00:25:03,768
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, it's this one, yeah, but now it's the other one.

296
00:25:04,068 --> 00:25:04,628
[SPEAKER_01]: So...

297
00:25:05,419 --> 00:25:09,061
[SPEAKER_01]: The one that you thought it was yours couldn't be yours, because now the other one is in its place.

298
00:25:09,881 --> 00:25:15,383
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's six... And then, within each of those domains of consciousness, you have infinite.

299
00:25:19,165 --> 00:25:24,487
[SPEAKER_00]: Infinite structure, isn't it?

300
00:25:24,547 --> 00:25:26,648
[SPEAKER_01]: Infinite direction, you can call it like that.

301
00:25:29,169 --> 00:25:30,770
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you look at a tree in the distance, eh...

302
00:25:31,663 --> 00:25:34,005
[SPEAKER_01]: Your consciousness is right there, at that distance.

303
00:25:34,145 --> 00:25:37,688
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't mean like your consciousness is there, as if you are here now.

304
00:25:38,008 --> 00:25:39,529
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you walk there, you'll see your consciousness.

305
00:25:39,589 --> 00:25:39,749
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

306
00:25:40,250 --> 00:25:45,094
[SPEAKER_01]: From your orientation right here, that distance there, the consciousness is out there.

307
00:25:45,534 --> 00:25:49,157
[SPEAKER_01]: And the extent the distance goes, the extent of the consciousness this goes.

308
00:25:50,778 --> 00:25:52,780
[SPEAKER_01]: Because otherwise, you wouldn't even perceive that.

309
00:25:52,880 --> 00:25:57,784
[SPEAKER_01]: You wouldn't even perceive the color or the difference of everything, if it's not manifested there as it is in the distance.

310
00:25:58,919 --> 00:26:02,400
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if that distance that is just perceived by itself, it's already conscious.

311
00:26:03,340 --> 00:26:04,520
[SPEAKER_01]: Consciousness is there.

312
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:06,000
[SPEAKER_01]: Distance is conscious.

313
00:26:06,301 --> 00:26:07,181
[SPEAKER_01]: Matter is conscious.

314
00:26:07,621 --> 00:26:09,081
[SPEAKER_01]: You just find it all there.

315
00:26:09,881 --> 00:26:11,922
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the only reason you can actually appropriate it.

316
00:26:13,282 --> 00:26:15,583
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the only reason why the Arahantship is possible.

317
00:26:16,603 --> 00:26:21,444
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you were not finding it there and appropriating it, you couldn't free yourself from it.

318
00:26:22,424 --> 00:26:27,245
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, if you are really creating consciousness and controlling it and directing it, that's it.

319
00:26:29,901 --> 00:26:32,362
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, there is no gap for any movement.

320
00:26:32,422 --> 00:26:34,123
[SPEAKER_01]: It's all sealed, closed, done.

321
00:26:35,403 --> 00:26:35,983
[SPEAKER_01]: And you're stuck.

322
00:26:36,863 --> 00:26:44,326
[SPEAKER_01]: The point being, no, there is a mistake going on, which is, you don't see that you already find things already there.

323
00:26:44,846 --> 00:26:45,606
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't see that.

324
00:26:46,346 --> 00:26:51,708
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you misconceive them as mine, as my creation, as I'm the master, as myself.

325
00:26:55,349 --> 00:26:57,310
[SPEAKER_01]: And what do you find already there?

326
00:26:57,750 --> 00:26:58,250
[SPEAKER_01]: Whatever

327
00:26:59,241 --> 00:27:00,722
[SPEAKER_01]: It has the nature of manifesting.

328
00:27:05,285 --> 00:27:20,456
[SPEAKER_01]: Even a fleeting thought, the fact that it has appeared, the fact that you did not... the fact that you just have it appear to you, means it came on its own.

329
00:27:22,858 --> 00:27:24,079
[SPEAKER_01]: To be honest, it's open on its own.

330
00:27:25,997 --> 00:27:27,278
[SPEAKER_01]: Same feeling, intention, anything.

331
00:27:27,298 --> 00:27:30,979
[SPEAKER_01]: The fact that it appears, means it did not come from you.

332
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:34,841
[SPEAKER_01]: You just met it.

333
00:27:34,861 --> 00:27:36,382
[SPEAKER_01]: Meeting of the three is contact.

334
00:27:39,423 --> 00:27:43,585
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you just met it, ignorantly, and you assumed you were contacted.

335
00:27:44,245 --> 00:27:44,926
[SPEAKER_01]: It is mine.

336
00:27:46,006 --> 00:27:46,506
[SPEAKER_01]: I am this.

337
00:27:47,107 --> 00:27:51,969
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you meet it with that understanding, that's... Well, yeah, then you're not contacted.

338
00:27:52,049 --> 00:27:54,510
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whatever, whatever manifests,

339
00:27:58,204 --> 00:28:00,726
[SPEAKER_01]: It's already there, given by itself, on its own.

340
00:28:01,687 --> 00:28:02,608
[SPEAKER_01]: You just find it there.

341
00:28:03,128 --> 00:28:08,112
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is nothing else than saying, whatever has the nature of arising, has the nature of ceasing.

342
00:28:09,333 --> 00:28:17,819
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, whatever is manifested, has the nature of manifestation, is in its nature independent of me.

343
00:28:19,881 --> 00:28:24,625
[SPEAKER_01]: And if something is independent of you, means it comes and goes, and you cannot do anything about it.

344
00:28:25,405 --> 00:28:29,789
[SPEAKER_01]: And if something is independent of you, it means it is not yours.

345
00:28:29,849 --> 00:28:31,790
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't obey you, it doesn't listen to you.

346
00:28:32,371 --> 00:28:33,552
[SPEAKER_00]: But you don't take anything.

347
00:28:35,153 --> 00:28:39,477
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you see that by default?

348
00:28:39,937 --> 00:28:45,242
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm seeing that it's... Yeah, all of these, the experimentation I'm talking about, it's just one insight, very much.

349
00:28:51,420 --> 00:29:02,628
[SPEAKER_00]: I do not say that there is... that there is the development of mindfulness of breathing for one who is forgetful.

350
00:29:10,314 --> 00:29:18,760
[SPEAKER_00]: For when he contemplates, I shall breathe in contemplating impermanence, contemplating, relinquish, fading away, cessation.

351
00:29:21,875 --> 00:29:30,160
[SPEAKER_00]: On that occasion, Abhikābhāna is contemplating mind-objects as mind-objects, having put away covetousness and grief for the world.

352
00:29:31,101 --> 00:29:39,366
[SPEAKER_00]: Having seen with wisdom the abandonment of covetousness and grief, he closely looks on with equanimity.

353
00:29:41,267 --> 00:29:43,388
[SPEAKER_00]: That is the occasion Abhikābhāna is contemplating.

354
00:29:51,518 --> 00:29:54,060
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that having seen it wasn't the abandoning of it.

355
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:57,082
[SPEAKER_00]: He knows, he sees it.

356
00:29:57,822 --> 00:30:01,124
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the result is indifference.

357
00:30:05,587 --> 00:30:07,248
[SPEAKER_00]: Establishing a minor indifference.

358
00:30:07,788 --> 00:30:08,389
[SPEAKER_00]: You get out, kid.

359
00:30:12,591 --> 00:30:13,072
[SPEAKER_00]: That's...

360
00:30:15,244 --> 00:30:23,992
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, see, the thing is, your mind needs to be quite strong already in order to establish... Yeah, because those are more refined phenomena.

361
00:30:25,233 --> 00:30:31,138
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, oh, stone or something like that, or body or material things, it's easier to relate to.

362
00:30:31,959 --> 00:30:34,662
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's how most people inevitably will have to start.

363
00:30:35,578 --> 00:30:49,384
[SPEAKER_01]: But yeah, if your mind gets established upon the thought... Well, you can get established to such a phenomenon, so general, so ambiguous, when you look at it from a daily kind of worldly point of view, like, just say, infinite consciousness.

364
00:30:50,764 --> 00:30:51,945
[SPEAKER_01]: But that is a real phenomenon.

365
00:30:52,465 --> 00:30:53,306
[SPEAKER_01]: It is real as such.

366
00:30:54,566 --> 00:30:58,908
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you see at the extent that it's present, which is very subtle,

367
00:31:01,299 --> 00:31:02,860
[SPEAKER_01]: And you get established upon that.

368
